## Public Projection

## Event

Christensen v. Harris County, No. 98-1167. Merits decision, May 1, 2000. Argued February 23, 2000. On certiorari to the Fifth Circuit, 158 F.3d 241, whose decision in No. 97-20796 was captioned Moreau v. Harris County. The questions are whether the Fair Labor Standards Act requires a specific agreement before a public employer may direct use of accrued compensatory time, and what weight the Labor Department's contrary opinion letter receives under the statute and regulations.

## Participation

Chief Justice Stone-Zsela and Justices Stevens, O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter, Thomas, Ginsburg and Breyer participated at argument and decision.

## Public Action

Affirmed.

## Judgment & Remedy

The Fifth Circuit's final judgment for the County and all other defendants is affirmed, 6–3. Supporting: Stone-Zsela, O'Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter and Thomas. Opposing: Stevens, Ginsburg and Breyer, who would set aside that judgment and remand for actual agreement coverage, terms and validity under a consent requirement.

The employees' categorical declaration and dependent $21,360 fee award remain displaced. The Court orders no agreement-specific proceedings, negotiations, trial, damages or new fee award. The policy remains subject to express statutory protections, binding agreements and other applicable law. Abandoned wrongful-refusal and retaliation claims are not revived.

